# Build context filter.
#
# The Dockerfile copies only pyproject.toml, README.md, uv.lock and ./app, but
# without this file the builder still tars the whole 1.6 GB working tree --
# .venv, .git, Terraform provider plugins, pytest/ruff caches. Beyond being
# slow, that is a correctness problem: a file that changes size while the
# context is being streamed makes podman fail the build with
# "archive/tar: write too long", which reads like a builder bug and is not.
#
# Keep this in sync with the COPY lines in the Dockerfile.

# Virtualenvs and Python build artefacts
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ty_cache/
.cache/

# VCS and local scratch
.git/
.gitignore
.run/

# Secrets and local configuration -- must never reach an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Infrastructure: Terraform state, provider plugins, Kubernetes manifests.
# None of it is needed at runtime, and state files carry connection details.
infra/

# Tests and docs
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Tooling configuration that only matters on a workstation
ruff.toml
ty.toml
pyrightconfig.json
Makefile
scripts/
